"""Evolve the ONE AA overview with current stock-system campaign evidence."""
from pathlib import Path
import json,html
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];page=ROOT.parent.parent/'project-overview.html';r=json.loads((ROOT/'results/campaign.json').read_text());rows=r['cases'];selected=r['selected_case'];prefix='Airflow-Assessment/system-study/'
tr=''.join('<tr>'+''.join(f'<td>{html.escape(str(v))}</td>' for v in [x['case'],f"{x['beta']:.1f}",f"{x['diameter_mm']:g} mm",f"{x['mass_g_s']:.2f} g/s",f"{x['nominal_dry_drop_c']:.2f}°C",f"{x['stress_min_drop_c']:.2f}°C",'pass' if x['numerically_accepted'] else 'FAIL'])+'</tr>' for x in rows)
start='<!-- system-study-start -->';end='<!-- system-study-end -->'
summary=(f"Current computational selection: <strong>{html.escape(selected['case'])}</strong>. Declared stress minimum <strong>{selected['stress_min_drop_c']:.2f}°C</strong>. "+('Meets the ≥7°C model margin.' if selected['passes_stress_plus_1C_margin'] else 'Does not meet the ≥7°C model margin.')) if selected else 'No numerical case qualifies for ranking yet.'
plots=''.join(f'<details><summary>{label}</summary><img src="{prefix}results/{name}.png" style="width:100%;max-width:1000px" alt="{label}"></details>' for name,label in [('source-operating-map','Paired stock source operating points'),('iteration-history','Executed iteration comparison'),('target-field','Selected target temperature field'),('nozzle-cad','Generated custom nozzle body')] if (ROOT/'results'/f'{name}.png').exists())
mesh=' '.join(f"{html.escape(m['coarse'])} vs {html.escape(m['fine'])}: {m['stress_drop_change_c']:.3f}°C stress-result change, "+('passes' if m['passes_0p5C_gate'] else 'FAILS')+' the 0.5°C mesh screen.' for m in r.get('mesh_comparisons',[])) or 'Mesh refinement for this operating point has not yet completed.'
block=f'''{start}
<section id="system-study"><div class="eyebrow">Active scope · stock components + custom nozzle · 19 Oct 2026</div><h2>Recursive system design without hardware</h2>
<p><strong>No hardware currently available.</strong> Historical test reports remain context. This campaign uses first principles, Lean, supplier maps, CFD and parametric CAD to build a computational shortlist. The target stays &gt;6°C across 5 × 5 cm at 20 cm, still air first. Proposed margin: ≥7°C under declared stresses.</p>
<p><strong>Build scope:</strong> stock compressor, receiver/cylinder, dryer, filter, regulator, valve, hose and vortex. The custom part is the low-pressure nozzle. Hypothetical turbine chains and custom pressure vessels do not enter the build shortlist. No shower construction.</p>
<img src="{prefix}results/system-architecture.png" style="width:100%" alt="Remote stock air supply feeds a local stock vortex and custom nozzle. Hot exhaust stays away from target.">
<div class="callout"><p>{summary}</p><p>{len(rows)} completed CFD cases in the saved campaign. {sum(x['numerically_accepted'] for x in rows)} pass numerical checks. This is a bounded search, not a physical or global optimum.</p></div>
<h3>What directs the next iteration</h3><div class="stateflow"><span>Stock source map<br>paired flow and temperature</span><b>→</b><span>CAD + CFD<br>geometry and changed flow</span><b>→</b><span>Quality gates<br>balances, residuals, fields</span><b>→</b><span>Lean + thermal screen<br>bounds, moisture, supply</span><b>→</b><span>Next candidate<br>source setting or nozzle size</span></div>
<p>The baseline uses the EXAIR approximate family curve at 100 psig with candidate model 3208. It replaces freely chosen flow/temperature pairs. Its application to a particular generator/assembly remains an assumption. Jeanoko has no verified source map and remains unranked. Manufacturer CAD and the actual EXAIR outlet interface are still needed for a fitted adapter.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table><tr><th>Case</th><th>Cold fraction</th><th>Outlet</th><th>Cold flow</th><th>Nominal dry drop</th><th>Stress minimum</th><th>Numerical gates</th></tr>{tr}</table></div>
<p>{mesh}</p>
<p>Selected nominal target speed: {selected.get('nominal_target_mean_speed_m_s',0):.2f} m/s. Nominal advected cold-deficit flux through the target: {selected.get('nominal_target_advected_deficit_w',0):.1f} W, before the one-way stresses. This is not heat removed from skin. With an illustrative fixed h=20 W/m²K, a 6°C improvement across 25 cm² would increase skin heat removal by only 0.30 W.</p>
<details><summary>Declared stress assumptions</summary><p>Source temperature drop reduced 20%; inlet 4°C above ambient; hot entrainment and wall surroundings 2°C above ambient; fresh CFD at 90% source flow; an extra 10% erosion of computed target fraction; U=20 W/m²K; 80% ambient RH; source pressure dew point +3°C. These are engineering screens, not measured tolerances or confidence intervals. Moisture and wall heating are one-way sensitivities.</p></details>
<details><summary>What the current CFD resolves</summary><p>Round internal cone and external jet, steady constant-density axisymmetric RANS, k-omega SST, transported source fraction. Each flow/geometry change is re-solved. It does not resolve buoyancy, 3D wind, hot exhaust, transient valves, wet walls, ice or a person. Seeds reuse fields only on identical geometry, then re-solve with unchanged acceptance checks.</p></details>
{plots}
<h3>Supply and architecture decisions</h3><p>Place the vortex near the custom nozzle. Carry compressed air through the long remote hose to avoid a long cold path. The Kaneez quoted 1000–1200 L/min passes the ideal mass budget for one source, but pressure-specific FAD and dryer dew point remain unverified. BAUER 100 L/min versus a 227 L/min source gives ≤44.1% ideal duty. A receiver changes peak flow; average production still limits duty. Neither option has an approved full installation here.</p>
<h3>First-principles formulation for presentations</h3><p>Mass, momentum and energy balances; isenthalpic regulators versus work-producing expansion; paired vortex maps; nozzle kinetic/static enthalpy; line heat pickup; area-average mixing; moist enthalpy; supply, duty and buffer inventory. Lean also checks the conservative area-envelope, nozzle energy and isothermal inventory identities. Editable equations are supplied as LaTeX expressions and slide-ready SVG/PNG.</p>
<details><summary>Concrete Lean certificate and parameter limits</summary><p>Effective area cold fraction ≥27%, cold source flow ≥2.4 g/s, UA ≤0.16 W/K, source contrast Tₑ−Tₛ ≥36 K, hot offset Tₑ−Tₐ ≤2 K and moisture warming ≤0.5 K imply ΔT ≥6.5396 K &gt;6 K. Lean derives retention ≥93% using exp(x)≥1+x, without a floating exponential. The source/CFD/moisture bounds remain hypotheses. <a href="{prefix}results/lean-envelope-check.json">Numerical hypothesis checks</a> · <a href="Airflow-Assessment/formal-model/AAThermo/System.lean">Kernel-checked system theorems</a>.</p></details>
<p><a href="{prefix}output/pdf/AA-first-principles-and-design.pdf">First-principles technical note PDF</a> · <a href="{prefix}FIRST-PRINCIPLES.txt">Editable derivation</a> · <a href="{prefix}results/equations/equations-latex.json">Equation source</a> · <a href="{prefix}cad/nozzle-flow-body.step">Nozzle STEP</a> · <a href="{prefix}cad/nozzle-print-mm.stl">Nozzle STL, mm</a> · <a href="{prefix}cad/nozzle-parametric.scad">Parametric CAD</a> · <a href="{prefix}results/campaign.json">Executed decisions and results</a> · <a href="{prefix}config.json">Search bounds and assumptions</a> · <a href="{prefix}README.txt">Reproduce and next tests</a> · <a href="Airflow-Assessment/AA-stock-system-study.zip">Source, evidence and CAD package</a></p>
<p><strong>Next computational gates:</strong> 3D variable density and buoyancy, 0.5/1 m/s crosswind, resolved hot exhaust and transient pulse response, then wall heating and person heat transfer. No hardware is needed to run these models. Physical source-map accuracy, fitted interface, noise and comfort remain later validation questions.</p>
<p class="sub">Primary component evidence: <a href="https://www.exair.com/vt.html">EXAIR</a> · <a href="https://www.bauer-kompressoren.de/de_de/junior-ii">BAUER</a>. Historical results elsewhere on this page keep their original operating assumptions.</p>
</section>{end}'''
s=page.read_text()
if start in s:
 a=s.index(start);b=s.index(end,a)+len(end);s=s[:a]+s[b:]
marker='<!-- formal-model-start -->';assert marker in s;s=s.replace(marker,block+'\n'+marker,1)
if 'href="#system-study"' not in s:s=s.replace('<nav aria-label="Sections">','<nav aria-label="Sections"><a href="#system-study">Stock system iteration</a>',1)
page.write_text(s);print(page)
